@startuml UC-SPRINT-TASK-CLAIM
' UC-25 - Claim Sprint Task | semantic key: UC-SPRINT-TASK-CLAIM
' Source: data/use_cases/sprint-work/UC-SPRINT-TASK-CLAIM.yml
' Business Rules: BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' Final nodes: F1 = task assigned to the Developer and recorded (postconditions met); F2 = claim
' rejected because another Developer claimed the task first, task not assigned to this Developer (EX-01).
' The UC defines no outcome for a task that fails the "active" part of NF2, so no branch is drawn for it.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|DEV| $lane_title("Developer")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|DEV|
start
' [NF1, TRIGGER, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER]
:Open unassigned task
and choose to claim it;
|SYS|
' [NF2, BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT]
:Verify task is active
and still unassigned;
if ($question("Task still unassigned?")) then ($guard_left("[unassigned]"))
  ' [NF3, POST1]
  :Assign task to Developer;
  ' [NF4, POST2]
  :Update Sprint Board
  and record assignment;
  stop
else ($guard_right("[claimed by another", "Developer — EX-01]"))
  ' [EX-01, GUIDE-7.3]
  :Reject task claim;
  stop
endif
@enduml
